riebel/Math/blob/4e635c77d7399d671ea58700e41bbd92cbdeeb46/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004435%2FFINAL_REVIEW_REQUEST.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/raw/4e635c77d7399d671ea58700e41bbd92cbdeeb46/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004435%2FFINAL_REVIEW_REQUEST.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/contents/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004435%2FFINAL_REVIEW_REQUEST.md?ref=4e635c77d7399d671ea58700e41bbd92cbdeeb46","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@\n+# Independent full five-turn review request\n+\n+Target30004435 / OWR-17474-009, Steif Question C, original printed632. Proposed result is unsolved5/5, with complete scoped entropy-free partials. Review all five proofs and the exact source, not only the computational receipts. The general source equality is known through entropy; the unresolved request is specifically a probability-only proof.\n+\n+## High-risk points to audit\n+\n+- Turn1: periodic phase versus invariant events; conditional D-stationarity; two-sided bridge denominator and uniform phase limits; completed-tail projection argument; ordered finite-window limits.\n+- Turn2: observability may merge hidden phases/classes; conditional empirical frequencies in both directions without reversibility; equal future profiles determine full laws using common D; word-length s−1 stabilization; stochastic-emission joint-state bound.\n+- Turn3: uniform-overlap and summable-continuity assumptions; forced agreement blocks and the stopping-time union bound; entire remote-future coupling rather than only a single coordinate; existence versus uniqueness; no unjustified bilateral-tail inference.\n+- Turn4: conull decisive-block definition; outside-only decoder measurability; exact summable boundary error; completed-field limit; radius moment is not automatic; inclusions do not equate two nontrivial subfields.\n+- Turn5: non-atomic disintegration, componentwise mixing with no uniform rate, joint L² profile recovery, countably many null sets, random law rather than redundant label; explicit irrational-rotation decoding in both directions and its nonmixing obstruction.\n+\n+## Replay and source instructions\n+\n+Run `python REPLAY_ALL.py` (stdlib only). Each TURN_n_CHECKS.json must match the corresponding script output byte-for-byte. The script also verifies historical and final artifact manifests. With `--sources PATH`, it verifies the PDF hashes in SOURCE_MANIFEST.json and TURN_3_SOURCE.json.\n+\n+Read the original Steif contribution pp632–633, especially Question C. Read Al-Najjar–Shmaya2014 Theorem5.2 pp13–14 and Example6.1. Read Lemańczyk2020 thesis AppendixB.1 andB.3.2 pp111–115 for entropy/Pinsker and finite-Markov scope. Read Bressaud–Fernández–Galves1999 Sections4.1–4.4 for coupling credit; the packet's stated total-variation criterion has its own proof. The raw sources are research inputs, not files for public upload.\n+\n+No theorem of unrestricted equality is claimed. A successful audit should bind exact frozen bytes and distinguish a scoped PASS from a resolution of the original method problem. Further author search has stopped at five turns; only additive source, review or packaging corrections should follow."},{"sha":"37bbeb6f3b53ae34ac18a594c4a4c24a6beebb59","filename":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30004435/PRIOR_GATE.json","status":"added","additions":15,"deletions":0,"changes":15,"blob_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/4e635c77d7399d671ea58700e41bbd92cbdeeb46/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004435%2FPRIOR_GATE.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/raw/4e635c77d7399d671ea58700e41bbd92cbdeeb46/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004435%2FPRIOR_GATE.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/contents/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004435%2FPRIOR_GATE.json?ref=4e635c77d7399d671ea58700e41bbd92cbdeeb46","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@\n+{\n+  \"id\": 30004435,\n+  \"result\": \"eligible; no accessible prior substantive attempt\",\n+  \"live_branches\": 409,\n+  \"recovered_remote_refs\": 379,\n+  \"checks\": [\n+    \"exact ID/code PRs\",\n+    \"tail field/tail sigma/Pinsker PR aliases\",\n+    \"live branch aliases\",\n+    \"recovered object paths and commit messages\",\n+    \"recovery inventory\",\n+    \"full pinned source record and null report\"\n+  ],\n+  \"limitations\": \"No exhaustive worldwide novelty/open-status claim; inaccessible deleted objects not certified absent.\"\n+}"},{"sha":"7a05b842d9c440adeb2751656abebe6a318b51dd","filename":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30004435/PR_BODY.md","status":"added","additions":17,"deletions":0,"changes":17,"blob_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/4e635c77d7399d671ea58700e41bbd92cbdeeb46/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004435%2FPR_BODY.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/raw/4e635c77d7399d671ea58700e41bbd92cbdeeb46/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004435%2FPR_BODY.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/contents/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004435%2FPR_BODY.md?ref=4e635c77d7399d671ea58700e41bbd92cbdeeb46","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@\n+## Result\n+\n+30004435 / OWR-17474-009: **unsolved, 5/5**, with an independent full scoped source/proof PASS.\n+\n+The equality of the one-sided tails is known through entropy theory. The original request specifically asks for a probability-only proof without entropy; this packet does not resolve that unrestricted method request.\n+\n+## Scoped progress\n+\n+Five genuine turns prove finite Markov class/phase classification, finite hidden-Markov observable-law quotients with a finite word certificate, a uniformly overlapping summably continuous infinite-memory coupling criterion, finite-mean finitary coding transfer, and non-atomic conditional-mixing mixture classification. Explicit weak-limit, coding and binary irrational-rotation examples identify limits of those reductions.\n+\n+All subclass assumptions and classical credit are retained. No bilateral-tail conclusion is inferred from mixing alone, and no original counterexample or novelty claim is made.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+All210,974 author assertions replay byte-for-byte, with166 author manifest entries and four source PDF hashes verified. The independent audit checks every proof and adds9,334 exact controls. Both replay commands are portable standard-library Python and documented in README.md.\n+\n+This draft preserves every frozen author/review byte, fresh-main ancestry and the final author WIP. Its diff is limited to this target folder and the target QUEUE status/turn cells. Raw sources and imported reports are excluded. No merge or release."},{"sha":"4d2d8e63877538b7c5629bda2ec7fbc08107afc4","filename":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30004435/PUBLICATION_MANIFEST.json","status":"added","additions":263,"deletions":0,"changes":263,"blob_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/4e635c77d7399d671ea58700e41bbd92cbdeeb46/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004435%2FPUBLICATION_MANIFEST.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/raw/4e635c77d7399d671ea58700e41bbd92cbdeeb46/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004435%2FPUBLICATION_MANIFEST.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/contents/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004435%2FPUBLICATION_MANIFEST.json?ref=4e635c77d7399d671ea58700e41bbd92cbdeeb46","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,263 @@\n+{\n+  \"problem_id\": 30004435,\n+  \"status\": \"unsolved5/5; scoped PASS only\",\n+  \"author_manifest_sha256\": \"48fce3e6630fd1bfd81c49054ab4c5640eeb7079f2bd6cc62b65ea479750d78c\",\n+  \"review_manifest_sha256\": \"fd9fdd983fc29b09fad2d2cc9c5264db782f0a6748404a639d837335f28aa5eb\",\n+  \"files\": [\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"FINAL_FROZEN_MANIFEST.json\",\n+      \"bytes\": 6354,\n+      \"sha256\": \"48fce3e6630fd1bfd81c49054ab4c5640eeb7079f2bd6cc62b65ea4